        "ggiEfTnnDeW_text": "&nbsp;The Most Misdiagnosed Condition In Women Aged 50-75? Gluteal Tendinopathy",
        "ggZeez2EarC_text": "<p><strong>If your hip pain is on the outer side —not deep in your groin—you likely have gluteal tendinopathy, not arthritis.</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Gluteal tendinopathy happens when the tendons connecting your hip muscles break down and become inflamed. <strong>75% of cases are misdiagnosed</strong> because doctors assume all hip pain is arthritis.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>While you get wrong treatments, your tendons break down faster than they can repair. <strong>Every month of misdiagnosis means more damage.</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>1 in 4 women over 50</strong> develop this—yet doctors completely miss it.</p>",
        "ggVpP4hdwHY_srcSet_desktop_src": "https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0810/1563/6283/files/20250829-103312.webp?v=1756441118",
