        "ggQct6zdn50_text": "<p><strong>Hip pain after 50 isn't \"normal aging\"—it's hormonal tendon breakdown.</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Here's what's really happening: <strong>Think of your tendons like strong rope cables holding your hip together. Low estrogen after 50 stops your body from making the \"glue\" (collagen) that keeps these cables strong.</strong> Without this repair, your hip tendons start fraying and become painful—like old rope that's losing its strength.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Why this hits women over 50 hardest:</strong> Your tendons need daily repair from movement and pressure. When hormones drop, even normal activities cause damage that won't heal.</p>",
